# Python Async Coding Guidelines

<purpose>
Follow all of these guidelines when programming async in python!
</purpose>


**Async Python:**

131. **Use `async`/`await` for non-blocking I/O**.
132. **Never block in async code**—use `await`, not `time.sleep()`.
133. **Use `asyncio.create_task()` for background tasks**.
134. **Limit concurrency with `asyncio.Semaphore` or queues**.
135. **Handle exceptions in async tasks explicitly**.
136. **Avoid mixing sync and async heavily**—keep layers clean.
137. **Use `aiohttp`, `aiomysql`, etc. for async-friendly libraries**.
138. **Benchmark async behavior with real workloads**.
139. **Test async code with `pytest-asyncio`**.
140. **Keep coroutines short and focused**.
